l modernize  and improve  border security and address the root  causes of immigration from central  america  in washington alexandra limon  one of the newest members of the nevada  legislature is also one of the youngest  ever state senator fabian danate is just  24 years old but already works in public  health  he's a democrat and was appointed to  replace ivana concello when she left  christian casadis has been interviewing  members of the hispanic legislative  caucus for us and  this week talked with state senator  danate  seeing the folks the republican side  there  just seeing how that you're going to  have to work with them  you know to get things done here um what  are some of the challenges what  you know what are you kind of seeing  here uh moving forward  i've been welcomed by the republican  side uh pretty warmly  they have been receptive to some of the  issues i have brought forth before them  i think that they understand the  jeopardy that our state is in right now  because of this public health crisis  and given my background in public health  they have been  understanding to some of the issues that  i'm trying to push forward  public health usually gets politicized  in some circumstances but for the most  part we're all fighting for the same  thing which is  to make sure that everyone is back to  their regular health that  we can reopen our schools and our  economies stabilize  anything kind of mapped out for the next  uh  few weeks or months yeah so my  legislation is going to prioritize  trying to fix and get us on the right  track  to solve this pandemic as have i as  i have already documented is that there  are  a lot of problems that stand in our way  to making sure that we  reach the threshold of making uh bring  everything back to normal  right now the greatest concern that we  have at this moment in time  is making sure that our communities are  vaccinated  and that we increase health literacy  which is the people actually understand  the information that is being received  to them  so the legislation that i want to put  forward is to increase uh  to allow employers for them to  pay their employees to get tested and  vaccinated so that they don't have to  worry about taking time off  to do that and any of the lost wages  that they might not be able to  recuperate that is going to be one of  the things that i try to entertain  within the next  few months and also expanding  translational services because as we  know  just not everyone has the ability to  speak in english within the state  and if we're able to communicate better  as to some of the outcomes of what can  be achieved through this vaccine  then we can start to fix a lot of the  public health issues that we are  recognizing right now at this moment  because of the pandemic  donate also said he wants to carry on  some of the priorities of his  predecessor ivana cancella  that includes pushing for drug pricing  transparency and bills that address  climate change
 

